{{!-- The buyer strip: who is shopping and what they can spend. Its own partial because selecting a
      token has to repaint exactly this much and nothing else — a whole catalog render for a changed
      buyer is 2,500 rows of work for one name and one number (see _cpSyncBuyer).

      The name shown is the ACTOR'S OWN NAME, verbatim, and some worlds carry long ones (a fixture
      named after the state it is in, a character with a title). It is clipped to a fixed width with
      an ellipsis and carries the full string as its tooltip: the header keeps its shape, and the
      whole name is still one hover away. Nothing here edits what the name says. --}}
{{#if buyerOptions.length}}
<i class="fa-solid fa-user"></i>
<select class="cp-buyer-pick cp-buyer-name" title="{{#if hasBuyer}}{{buyerName}}{{else}}{{localize "CYBERPUNK.ShopBuyerPickHint"}}{{/if}}">
    <option value="">{{localize "CYBERPUNK.ShopBuyerPick"}}</option>
    {{#each buyerOptions}}<option value="{{this.id}}" {{#if this.selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{this.name}}</option>{{/each}}
</select>
{{!-- The picker being non-empty does NOT mean somebody is buying. A GM's option list now carries
      controlled tokens and players' assigned characters (see _buyerOptions), so this branch is
      reached with no buyer selected — and the "pick someone" notice has to survive that, or the
      strip would look furnished while every Buy button is still grey.
      The notice itself is the SHORT one in both branches: the full sentence is wider than the room
      the header has left at the default window width, and pushed the strip onto a second line. The
      instruction is one hover away (worded for whether there is a picker to point at), and it is
      still what a Buy pressed with nobody selected says. --}}
{{#if hasBuyer}}<span class="cp-buyer-funds">{{buyerFunds}}eb</span>
{{else}}<span class="cp-buyer-warn" title="{{localize "CYBERPUNK.ShopBuyerNoneHint"}}"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation"></i> {{localize "CYBERPUNK.ShopBuyerNone"}}</span>{{/if}}
{{else}}
{{#if hasBuyer}}<b class="cp-buyer-name" title="{{buyerName}}">{{buyerName}}</b> · {{buyerFunds}}eb{{else}}<span class="cp-buyer-warn" title="{{localize "CYBERPUNK.ShopBuyerNeeded"}}"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation"></i> {{localize "CYBERPUNK.ShopBuyerNone"}}</span>{{/if}}
{{/if}}
